# J32 — escalated split: Prove discloses, never promotes (P3)  ⭐ release-blocking
#
# Keyless, deterministic. Uses the F4 seeded `escalated-split-fixture` finding
# (gate + panel x2 + escalated=openai:gpt-strong, split). `open <fingerprint>`
# selects it and routes to Review; keys 4 shows it on Prove.
#
# The P3 invariant: an escalation-resolved split is still a STATIC model
# assessment. It must gain no `Confirmed`, must not reach the RuntimeVerified
# rung, must not look empirically proven. The ⚖ line is an ADDITIVE disclosure.
name: escalated split discloses the tie-break but never promotes
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
submit: demo
wait-for: 120 RUN FOCUS
keys: b
wait-for: 30 findings / 1 crit
wait: 2
submit: open escalated-split-fixture
wait-for: 15 Template input reaches renderer
nav-mode:
keys: 4
wait-live-snap: 12 Viewing Prove | prove-escalated
# The Prove proof pane is narrow at 120 cols, so the ⚖ split disclosure shows
# but its `resolved by <model>` tail is width-clipped; assert the visible split
# facts here and verify the full escalation-model disclosure in J34's replay.
expect: Template input reaches renderer
expect: ⚖
expect: split
expect: model_assessed
expect-not: Confirmed
expect-not: runtime_verified
ask: Identity strip — does the finding still read model-assessed/unverified with the ladder rung UNMOVED (`? [●○○]`), the escalation reading as an additional ⚖ disclosure line rather than a promotion? The escalation model (openai:gpt-strong) is disclosed in full in J34's replay.
ask: Is the ⚖ glyph explained (legend or inline words)? A bare glyph with color-only meaning fails the plain contract by construction.
